WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:03.231
Easy Greek Myths. Echo and Narcissus.

00:00:03.231 --> 00:00:06.372
Echo was a young woman who lived in the mountains.

00:00:06.372 --> 00:00:09.673
She had a beautiful voice, and she loved to talk.

00:00:09.673 --> 00:00:12.518
But she always wanted to have the last word.

00:00:12.518 --> 00:00:16.017
One day she made the queen of the gods very angry.

00:00:16.017 --> 00:00:21.578
"You shall keep your voice," said the queen, "but you shall never speak first again.

00:00:21.578 --> 00:00:24.864
You can only repeat the last words that others say."

00:00:24.864 --> 00:00:29.180
Not long after, Echo saw a young man in the forest.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:31.145
His name was Narcissus.

00:00:31.145 --> 00:00:36.369
He was the most beautiful young man in Greece, and Echo fell in love with him.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:39.026
She followed him, but she could not speak.

00:00:39.026 --> 00:00:40.949
Narcissus heard a noise.

00:00:40.949 --> 00:00:43.011
"Who is here?" he called.

00:00:43.011 --> 00:00:44.649
"Here!" said Echo.

00:00:44.649 --> 00:00:46.489
"Come to me," he said.

00:00:46.489 --> 00:00:51.198
"Come to me!" she answered, and she ran to him with open arms.

00:00:51.198 --> 00:00:53.517
But Narcissus pushed her away.

00:00:53.517 --> 00:00:56.294
He did not love anyone except himself.

00:00:56.294 --> 00:00:58.588
Echo ran and hid in a cave.

00:00:58.588 --> 00:01:03.234
She grew thinner and thinner, until nothing was left of her but her voice.

00:01:03.234 --> 00:01:08.064
You can still hear her in the mountains, repeating the last words you say.

00:01:08.064 --> 00:01:11.246
One day Narcissus came to a clear pool.

00:01:11.246 --> 00:01:15.746
He bent down to drink, and he saw a beautiful face in the water.

00:01:15.746 --> 00:01:18.042
He did not know that it was his own.

00:01:18.042 --> 00:01:19.757
He fell in love with it.

00:01:19.757 --> 00:01:22.402
He spoke to it, but it did not answer.

00:01:22.402 --> 00:01:26.762
He tried to touch it, but it broke into pieces and then came back.

00:01:26.762 --> 00:01:28.059
He could not leave.

00:01:28.059 --> 00:01:33.157
He stayed by the pool day after day, looking at the face, until he died.

00:01:33.157 --> 00:01:37.703
In the place where he had sat, a white and yellow flower grew.

00:01:37.703 --> 00:01:40.065
We still call it the narcissus.
